title: 'eth-rpc: add a CLI option to rate-limit the historical block sync'
doc:
- audience: [Node Dev, Node Operator]
  description: |-
    eth-rpc has a new option, `--historical-sync-max-blocks-per-sec <N>`, that limits the
    historical block sync to at most `N` blocks per second on average, to reduce the load on the
    node. It requires `--eth-pruning archive` (the default); with any other value, eth-rpc fails
    to start. Without the option there is no limit, so existing deployments need no change.

    eth-rpc also logs its stored sync state at startup.

    `CliCommand` has a new public field, `historical_sync_max_blocks_per_sec`. Code that constructs
    it with a struct literal must set the field; `None` keeps the previous behavior.
crates:
- name: pallet-revive-eth-rpc
  bump: major
